config INPUT_IQS9151_TOUCH_STATE_ENABLE
    bool "IQS9151 raw touch state event"
    default n
    help
      Emit a key event whenever a finger touches or leaves the trackpad,
      independent of gesture detection. On a split keyboard only processed
      input events are relayed between halves, so enabling this on one half
      lets the other half react to "that pad is being touched" - for example
      to hold a layer while the other hand rests on its trackpad.

config INPUT_IQS9151_TOUCH_STATE_CODE
    int "IQS9151 touch state event code"
    depends on INPUT_IQS9151_TOUCH_STATE_ENABLE
    default 264
    help
      Input event code reported for the touch state. Defaults to 264
      (INPUT_BTN_8), which is not used by any of the gesture events
      (BTN_0..BTN_7).

config INPUT_IQS9151_TOUCH_STATE_2F_CODE
    int "IQS9151 two-finger touch state event code"
    depends on INPUT_IQS9151_TOUCH_STATE_ENABLE
    default 265
    help
      Input event code reported while two or more fingers are on the pad.
      Defaults to 265 (INPUT_BTN_9). Reported alongside the single-finger
      touch state, so two fingers raise both codes.

